in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @spectral/gen_prism
in @uuid/spectral
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/au
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @spectral/supervisor — the lifecycle-owner primitive.
#
# THE SECOND SUB-SHARD of the @spectral runtime cascade. Sibling
# of `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` (commit ae965ca, the worker
# primitive). Lifts the @beam-altitude `supervisor` declaration
# (boot/std/beam.mirror; the existing strategy / supervisor pair) to
# the substrate altitude under the @spectral family root, and names
# the BEAM gen_server/supervisor pair as one closed pair at the
# substrate altitude.
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 (2026-06-10, Mara): a
# `supervisor` is a `gen_prism` specialisation. Its state surface
# is a `registry` shard (a content-addressed index from child
# `uuid_spectral` to child shard ref); its tool surface is the
# lifecycle API (`start_child`, `terminate_child`, restart per the
# strategy); its invariant is a restart-strategy contract analogous
# to BEAM's `:one_for_one` / `:one_for_all` / `:rest_for_one`.
#
# === The keyword decision ===
#
# `glass` per recognition #46 (path-syntax property; promoted) and
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s discipline section: "@spectral
# sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass`; the family root itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline."
#
# Why NOT a new substrate keyword: supervisor is a sub-prism
# specialisation of gen_prism — the BEAM `:supervisor` behaviour
# analogue — and `glass` already names that relationship per
# `shards/glass.mirror`'s `glass(name) -> prism` form. Same logic as
# `@spectral/gen_prism` (commit ae965ca): not a new structural kind,
# but a specialisation of an existing one (gen_prism specialises
# prism; supervisor specialises gen_prism). No `declared_keywords`
# extension needed.
#
# === Specialisation, not extension ===
#
# Mirror has no `T + {fields}` syntax for type extension. The
# supervisor IS-A gen_prism relationship is structural-by-embedding:
# the supervisor record carries the gen_prism record in a `base`
# field. The five-op tool surface comes through the `glass
# @spectral/supervisor` declaration (per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]); the gen_prism's
# three surfaces (identity, state, parent) reach through `base`. The
# BEAM precedent is `type supervisor(children) { <process, ... }`
# (boot/std/beam.mirror) where `<process` is the boot-floor
# composition syntax; modern shards use embedded `base: T` fields,
# which is what this shard adopts.
#
# === The registry shard — gen_prism.state IS the registry ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: the supervisor's state
# surface IS its registry shard. The gen_prism.state field
# (a `shard_ref`, i.e. `uuid_spectral`) on the supervisor's `base`
# already carries this — the supervisor's state IS a content-
# addressed registry mapping each child's `uuid_spectral` to that
# child's current shard ref.
#
# The dedicated registry shard (`shards/spectral/registry.mirror`)
# carries the registry's typed surface (lookup-by-uuid, enumerate
# children, observe child state). This shard does NOT inline the
# registry contract; it forward-promises it. The supervisor's
# `base.state: shard_ref` field is the substrate-altitude handle to
# the registry shard at runtime; the dedicated shard fills in the
# query surface in a later cascade tick.
#
# Substrate-pull rationale for the forward-promise (NOT a STOP):
# the supervisor declaration's load-bearing surface (start_child,
# terminate_child, the strategy contract) does NOT depend on the
# registry's query API. The registry's QUERY surface is a separate
# consumer pull; the supervisor's LIFECYCLE surface lands here. The
# state surface is typed as `shard_ref` (the existing carrier);
# downstream consumers that need registry query lift through the
# dedicated registry shard when that tick lands.
#
# === Strategy — three closed variants, NOT four ===
#
# Per `boot/std/beam.mirror` (the existing BEAM-altitude precedent):
#
#   type strategy = one_for_one | one_for_all | rest_for_one
#
# Three closed variants. The brief's sketch listed four including
# `simple_one_for_one`; substrate-pull-correct decision (architectural
# call surfaced here): drop `simple_one_for_one`. Modern OTP
# deprecated `:simple_one_for_one` in favour of `DynamicSupervisor`
# (Elixir, OTP 19+) — the substrate's own precedent already names
# only the three durable strategies. Carrying a deprecated variant
# at the substrate altitude would proliferate dead vocabulary the
# BEAM altitude already pruned. When the substrate wants dynamic-
# child semantics, it lifts the modern `DynamicSupervisor`
# discipline as its own sub-prism (separate tick); this shard does
# not pre-commit to that vocabulary.
#
# This matches the @beam shard's precedent at the substrate
# altitude. The recognition #58 PROMOTED rule (substrate-already-
# had-the-word) applies: the strategy carrier was already named at
# @beam; this shard lifts the same closed set to the @spectral
# altitude under the supervisor specialisation.
#
# === child_spec — the supervisor's configuration list ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 and the BEAM `:child_spec`
# analogue. The supervisor's invariant fires on each child against
# its child_spec entry. Fields:
#
#   id          — the child's uuid_spectral (the substrate's
#                  content-addressed identity carrier; the
#                  registry's lookup key);
#   start       — the gen_prism declaration's identity. The
#                  supervisor invokes `@spectral/gen_prism.start`
#                  against this `uuid_spectral` to spawn the child.
#                  Carrier choice rationale: mirror has no
#                  substrate-altitude `action` type for first-class
#                  start-functions (BEAM's {Module, Function, Args}
#                  has no clean substrate analogue) — the substrate-
#                  pull-correct carrier is the content address of
#                  the gen_prism's declaration shard. The autopoietic
#                  identity surface (per boot/std/mirror/runtime/
#                  gen_prism.mirror's `name: zoom(oid, gen_prism)`
#                  fixed point, lifted to uuid_spectral per
#                  shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror) IS the start
#                  reference;
#   restart     — the per-child restart policy (permanent /
#                  temporary / transient — the BEAM precedent;
#                  closed sum below);
#   shutdown    — the graceful-shutdown deadline. After this
#                  deadline elapses on a terminate request, the
#                  child is killed without further pre-shutdown
#                  cleanup. `duration` from
#                  @epistemologic/reality/time (settle({ nanos:
#                  u64 })); the substrate's unified time discipline
#                  per recognition #25 (the substrate's own time
#                  family migration, 2026-06-06);
#   kind        — child type discriminator (worker / supervisor —
#                  the BEAM precedent; closed sum below). A
#                  `worker` child terminates as a normal exit;
#                  a `supervisor` child cascades termination to
#                  its own subtree before exiting.
#
# === restart_kind — closed sum ===
#
# Per BEAM's `:restart` field (permanent | temporary | transient):
#
#   permanent  — always restart on exit (the default for long-
#                running services);
#   temporary  — never restart on exit (one-shot tasks);
#   transient  — restart only on abnormal exit (au carrying a
#                failure verdict per @glass; normal-exit au's
#                stay terminated).
#
# Substrate-pull-correct semantics: the supervisor's restart
# decision IS a kintsugi morphism evaluated against the child's
# terminate-au under the per-child restart_kind. The morphism's
# discriminator is the child's terminate-au verdict; the
# restart_kind gates whether the morphism fires. Body discharges
# through @kintsugi at the supervisor altitude.
#
# === child_kind — closed sum ===
#
# Per BEAM's `:type` field (worker | supervisor). Mirrored at the
# substrate altitude; named `child_kind` to disambiguate from
# `type` (the substrate keyword).
#
#   worker      — leaf gen_prism. Normal terminate-au settles into
#                 the parent's registry shard;
#   supervisor  — branch gen_prism. Terminate cascades: each child
#                 of THIS supervisor terminates first; THIS
#                 supervisor's terminate-au is settled only after
#                 the cascade closes. Per docs/specs/spectral-
#                 runtime.md §3's parentage-is-acyclic invariant,
#                 the cascade is bounded.
#
# === Lifecycle surface — start_child / terminate_child ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3:
#
#   start_child   — spawn a child under the supervisor; the child's
#                   parent edge is set to the supervisor; the
#                   registry shard advances by one settle (the
#                   child's uuid_spectral + shard ref is appended
#                   to the registry's settled state). Body
#                   discharges by invoking
#                   `@spectral/gen_prism.start(supervisor.base)`
#                   against the child_spec.start uuid_spectral.
#
#   terminate_child — terminate a child under the supervisor; the
#                   child's terminate-au settles into the registry
#                   shard (transitioning the child's registry view
#                   from `running` to `terminated`). Returns `au`
#                   carrying the final delta. Body discharges
#                   through @kintsugi at the supervisor altitude
#                   (the terminate is one of the three lifecycle
#                   events the supervisor owns per gen_prism's
#                   spec).
#
# The supervisor's RESTART action is NOT a separate surface action.
# Restart is the automatic substrate-pull-correct transformation
# under the supervision invariant: when a child gen_prism's
# `terminate() -> au` settles with a failure verdict (per @glass's
# imperfect family) AND the child's child_spec.restart gates
# restart-on-this-au (the BEAM permanent/transient discriminator),
# the supervisor fires `@spectral/gen_prism.restart()` against the
# child. This is a kintsugi-morphism-driven transformation, not a
# caller-invoked surface action; the substrate's restart logic IS
# the kintsugi morphism per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3.
#
# === The mara-spawn example resolved ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §4: when Mara spawns to work
# on mirror's substrate, the spawn's parent is `~/.mara/`
# gen_prism (the supervisor lifecycle owner) and the spawn is
# ENTANGLED with mirror's repo gen_prism (the peer-correlation
# edge, declared at `shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror` —
# forward-promised). The supervisor only acts on the parent edge;
# entanglement is orthogonal to this shard's surface.
#
# === Honest partial discipline (per #306) ===
#
# The action bodies below all carry `\` obligation blocks — no
# fracture body emits any morphism in this tick. No `partials`
# declaration needed (per `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`
# #306). Bodies discharge downstream when the consumer pulls
# realisation through `@code/metalogue/materialize` (per the
# ouroboros pipeline in docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §5).
#
# === Cascade siblings (forward-promised, NOT landing this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/registry.mirror       supervisor's child
#                                          registry; query surface
#                                          (lookup by uuid_spectral;
#                                          enumerate children;
#                                          observe child state);
#   shards/spectral/parent.mirror         single-parent lifecycle
#                                          edge type (acyclic);
#   shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror   peer correlation edge;
#                                          sheaf restriction map at
#                                          substrate altitude;
#   shards/spectral/root.mirror           parentless supervisor;
#                                          vocabulary anchor at
#                                          ~/.mirror/;
#   shards/spectral/portal.mirror         runtime side of portal
#                                          (gen_prism specialisation
#                                          carrying the frame stream).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (the ouroboros
#               spec; §3 supervision tree; §8 cascade map),
#               boot/std/beam.mirror (the @beam-altitude strategy /
#               supervisor precedent at the BEAM altitude that this
#               shard lifts).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]] (the
#                      per-shard memory manager named for Margaret
#                      Hamilton; the supervisor altitude where
#                      Apollo-1202 priority discipline lives),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the registry
#                      state surface IS a shard; restart-driven
#                      registry transitions ARE lattice ascent),
#                      [[architecture-error-as-question]] (Reflection
#                      threshold convergence on Beer/Reyes/BEAM that
#                      grounds the substrate-pull-correct restart
#                      decision),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the supervisor name lived in boot/std/beam.mirror
#                      under @beam since the early boot; this tick
#                      lifts it to the substrate altitude under the
#                      @spectral family root — the 53rd-instance
#                      rug-pull).
# Related shards: spectral.mirror (the family root this glass is
#                  under),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the worker primitive
#                  this glass specialises; commit ae965ca),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the identity carrier; child
#                  ids ARE uuid_spectrals),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the state-surface carrier;
#                  shard_ref = uuid_spectral),
#                 mirror/au.mirror (the proposed-shard carrier;
#                  terminate_child's return shape),
#                 epistemologic/reality/time.mirror (the duration
#                  carrier; shutdown deadlines).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror` declares
# `@spectral/supervisor` and only that.

glass @spectral/supervisor {
  focus supervisor
  project supervisor
  split supervisor
  shift supervisor
  settle supervisor
}

# === restart_kind — per-child restart policy ===
#
# Closed sum gating the supervisor's restart decision against the
# child's terminate-au verdict. Per BEAM's `:restart` precedent.
#
#   permanent  — always restart on exit;
#   temporary  — never restart on exit;
#   transient  — restart only on abnormal exit.
type restart_kind =
  | permanent
  | temporary
  | transient

# === child_kind — child-type discriminator ===
#
# Closed sum naming whether the child is a leaf (worker) or
# branch (supervisor) gen_prism. Drives the terminate cascade:
# a `supervisor` child cascades termination to its subtree before
# its own terminate-au settles. Per BEAM's `:type` field (renamed
# to `child_kind` to disambiguate from the substrate's `type`
# keyword).
type child_kind =
  | worker
  | supervisor

# === restart_strategy — the supervision invariant ===
#
# Closed sum naming the supervisor's response when a child fails.
# Lifts `boot/std/beam.mirror`'s `type strategy = one_for_one |
# one_for_all | rest_for_one` to the substrate altitude under the
# @spectral family root.
#
#   one_for_one   — restart only the failed child;
#   one_for_all   — restart all children when one fails;
#   rest_for_one  — restart the failed child and all children
#                   declared after it in child_specs.
#
# NOT `simple_one_for_one`: the substrate-pull-correct decision
# (recognition #58 PROMOTED — substrate-already-had-the-word) is
# to match the @beam shard's three-variant precedent. Modern OTP
# deprecated `:simple_one_for_one` in favour of `DynamicSupervisor`
# (Elixir, OTP 19+); the dynamic-child discipline lifts in its own
# substrate tick when its first consumer surfaces.
type restart_strategy =
  | one_for_one
  | one_for_all
  | rest_for_one

# === child_spec — the per-child configuration entry ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 and the BEAM `:child_spec`
# precedent. Each entry in the supervisor's `child_specs` list
# names one supervised gen_prism.
#
#   id        — the child's uuid_spectral (identity at the
#                substrate altitude; the registry's lookup key);
#   start     — the content address of the gen_prism declaration
#                the supervisor spawns. The supervisor invokes
#                `@spectral/gen_prism.start` against this
#                uuid_spectral; the autopoietic fixed point per
#                shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror is the substrate
#                guarantee that the address resolves uniquely to
#                the declaration shard;
#   restart   — the per-child restart policy (closed sum above);
#   shutdown  — the graceful-shutdown deadline. `duration` from
#                @epistemologic/reality/time (u64 nanoseconds,
#                non-negative-by-settle-witness);
#   kind      — child-type discriminator (closed sum above).
type child_spec = {
  id:       uuid_spectral,
  start:    uuid_spectral,
  restart:  restart_kind,
  shutdown: duration,
  kind:     child_kind,
}

# === supervisor — the lifecycle-owner record ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: a `supervisor` is a
# `gen_prism` specialisation. The `base` field carries the
# embedded gen_prism (identity, state, parent surfaces); the
# supervisor adds the configuration list and the restart-strategy
# invariant.
#
# The state surface (base.state: shard_ref) IS the registry shard:
# a content-addressed index from child uuid_spectral to child
# shard ref. Restart-driven transitions ARE lattice ascent (per
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]); the registry's settled state
# advances by one settle per supervised lifecycle event.
#
# The dedicated `shards/spectral/registry.mirror` (forward-
# promised) declares the registry's query surface (lookup-by-
# uuid, enumerate children, observe child state). This shard's
# `base.state` typing as `shard_ref` (the existing carrier) is the
# substrate-altitude handle; the registry's typed surface arrives
# in a later cascade tick.
type supervisor = {
  base:             gen_prism,
  child_specs:      [child_spec],
  restart_strategy: restart_strategy,
}

# === start_child — supervisor-initiated child spawn ===
#
# The supervisor's request to spawn a child gen_prism under a
# given child_spec. The child's parent edge is set to the
# supervisor (the supervisor IS the parent at this lifecycle
# event); the registry shard advances by one settle (the child's
# uuid_spectral + shard ref is appended to the registry's settled
# state).
#
# Body discharges by invoking `@spectral/gen_prism.start` against
# the child_spec.start uuid_spectral: the autopoietic fixed point
# resolves the declaration shard, the gen_prism constructor fires,
# the parent edge is set, the registry's settle advances. The body
# stays a `\` obligation in this tick; concrete resolution lives at
# the realisation layer (via @code/metalogue/materialize per the
# ouroboros pipeline).
start_child(s: supervisor, spec: child_spec) -> gen_prism { \ }

# === terminate_child — supervisor-initiated child termination ===
#
# Terminate a child under the supervisor. The child's `terminate()
# -> au` (per shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror) settles into the
# registry shard, transitioning the child's registry view from
# `running` to `terminated`. Returns `au` carrying the final
# delta; the supervisor's registry shard advances by one lattice
# element.
#
# Bounded by child_spec.shutdown: if the child fails to terminate
# within the deadline, the supervisor forces termination (the
# substrate-pull-correct enforcement under the supervision
# invariant; body discharges through @kintsugi at the supervisor
# altitude).
terminate_child(s: supervisor, id: uuid_spectral) -> au { \ }

out @spectral/supervisor
out restart_kind
out child_kind
out restart_strategy
out child_spec
out supervisor
out start_child
out terminate_child
